DIKUMUD LICENSE

    This document contains the rules by which you can use, alter or publish
parts of DikuMud. DikuMud has been created by the following five people:

   Katja Nyboe               (katz@freja.diku.dk)
   Tom Madsen                (noop@freja.diku.dk)
   Hans Henrik Staerfeldt    (bombman@freja.diku.dk)
   Michael Seifert           (seifert@freja.diku.dk)
   Sebastian Hammer          (quinn@freja.diku.dk)

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
    
    DikuMud is a substantial portion of the development time of these five
people during the last year, and is provided as such. We would like to see
something in return. This is NOT money, since this product is meant to be
free to everyone. We would like to see a lot of active, interesting, and
creative games developed, and would like to know about them. We would also
like to know that our work has been useful to you, and that you appreciate
our efforts.

Therefore, the rules are as follows:

1. You may NOT use DikuMud to make money in ANY way. This includes charging
   users to play, accepting donations for in-game benefits, or selling any
   part of the code or documentation.

2. You may alter the code in any way you wish, provided that you retain the
   original copyright notices in all files, and that you do not remove the
   names of the original authors from the login sequence or the 'credits'
   command.

3. If you distribute a modified version of DikuMud, you must include this
   license document intact, and you must clearly state that your version is
   derived from DikuMud.

4. You must notify the DikuMud authors if you put up a publicly accessible
   game based on DikuMud.

5. DikuMud is provided "as is", without any warranty of any kind, either
   expressed or implied. The authors are not liable for any damages arising
   from the use of this software.
